{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,23]],"date-time":"2026-10-23T20:25:43Z","timestamp":1792787143783,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"SPIE-Intl Soc Optical Eng","issue":"04","funder":[{"name":"Semiconductor R&D Center, Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd","id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/020m7t761","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Micro\/Nanopattern. Mats. Metro."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,17]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) imaging plays a crucial role in metrology and inspection (MI) systems across various fields, including semiconductor manufacturing and nanotechnology. This method benefits for providing detailed surface and compositional analysis with a high-quality (HQ) image. Yet, producing HQ images with SEM imaging not only requires a long acquisition time but also introduces new challenges for maintaining reasonable throughput, which potentially disrupts the MI workflows. To leverage the semiconductor industry with a better approach, we propose an effective artificial-intelligence-powered image enhancement solution, namely, MI-image enhancement solution (MI-IES), that integrates deep learning techniques. MI-IES is designed to enhance the efficiency of massive metrology applications within MI workflows by processing low-quality SEM images as an input target and subsequently processing them using image enhancement algorithms. Specifically, MI-IES contains two main modules: super-resolution and denoising, to overcome the stated challenges in our study. Extensive experiments across various actual devices were conducted using SEM imaging. The results highlight MI-IES enhanced capability in massive metrology applications, as evidenced by the superior R2 analysis that yielded a score \u22650.90 in terms of SEM image quality. In addition, MI-IES achieved remarkable throughput processing time by a decrease of up to 75% (3.9 times faster) in comparison to HQ, underscoring its efficiency. Our solution not only delivers superior performance but also benefits massive metrology with sufficient throughput and high structural integrity of the SEM imaging.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1117\/1.jmm.24.4.041407","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,17]],"date-time":"2025-10-17T06:26:02Z","timestamp":1760682362000},"page":"1-18","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["AI-powered super-resolution and denoising of scanning electron microscopy images for high-throughput metrology and inspection"],"prefix":"10.1117","volume":"24","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3786-2117","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Leslie Ching Ow","family":"Tiong","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jhongkwon","family":"Kim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Daewon","family":"Choi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chaehoon","family":"Park","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Junhui","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Songhyun","family":"Yu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yeny","family":"Yim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SAMSUNG Electronics Co., Ltd."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wonhee","f